Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:59:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] blk/virtio: negotiate VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1

The driver uses the modern transport (MMIO version 2, PCI common config) but accepted no
features, VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1 included. QEMU then treats the device as legacy when it restores a
snapshot and recomputes the avail and used rings' addresses from the descriptor table's: the
device completes requests into a ring the driver never reads.
---
 drivers/blk/virtio/block.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/blk/virtio/block.c b/drivers/blk/virtio/block.c
index 1a19cdfa..99e26a43 100644
--- a/drivers/blk/virtio/block.c
+++ b/drivers/blk/virtio/block.c
@@ -308,7 +308,10 @@ void virtio_blk_init(void)
 #endif
     /* Select features we want from the device */
     virtio_transport_set_driver_features(&dev, 0, 0);
-    virtio_transport_set_driver_features(&dev, 1, 0);
+    /* VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1: a modern transport's device needs it; without it QEMU treats the device
+     * as legacy when restoring a snapshot and recomputes the rings' addresses */
+    virtio_transport_set_driver_features(&dev, 1, virtio_transport_get_device_features(&dev, 1)
+                                                  & (1u << (VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1 - 32)));
 
     virtio_transport_set_status(&dev, VIRTIO_DEVICE_STATUS_FEATURES_OK);
     if (!(virtio_transport_get_status(&dev) & VIRTIO_DEVICE_STATUS_FEATURES_OK)) {
